    type: 'CR',
    section: 'Verbal',
    difficulty: 'hard',
    topic: 'Assumption',
    question: 'Researchers found that students who sleep at least 8 hours per night score, on average, 15% higher on standardized cognitive tests than students who sleep fewer than 6 hours. A school district concluded from this data that mandating later school start times, to allow students to sleep longer, will improve student academic performance. Which of the following is an assumption upon which the conclusion depends?',
