    explanation: 'The argument: evidence (more sleep → better test scores) → intervention (later start times) → outcome (better academic performance). The key gap: will later start times actually result in more sleep? This only works if students currently sleep less because of early start times. (B) is the critical assumption: if students sleep fewer than 8 hours for reasons unrelated to school start times (late-night social media, part-time jobs, etc.), then later start times will not increase sleep duration, and the intervention will fail. (A) is about whether the tests measure what they claim — relevant but not the primary logical gap in this argument. (C) is about stakeholder support — an implementation concern, not a logical assumption. (D) is about cost-benefit justification — a practical concern separate from whether the intervention works at all. (E) is about whether the problem is widespread — establishes scope but not whether the intervention will work. Trap: (E) seems necessary (why intervene if most students sleep enough?) but the argument\'s logic does not depend on this — even a minority could justify the policy. Target: 2:00',
