    question: 'A technology startup that develops autonomous delivery robots has been operating in three pilot cities. In City A, where sidewalks are wide and well-maintained, delivery success rates exceed 95%. In City B, where sidewalks are narrower and have frequent obstacles, success rates are 72%. In City C, where the startup was required to pay high municipal licensing fees, it withdrew operations after two months due to financial losses, despite the physical infrastructure being similar to City A. Which of the following can be most properly inferred from this information?',
